Verify the selection against current_kernel, skills, and exclude_skills in the
generation record. Read files with klineage.memory.load_skill or reconstruct inline
SkillCards. Do not modify any files.
Counter profiles currently support CUDA only; HIP or Ascend event timings are
insufficient evidence for profile-based ranking.

Recompute eligible cards with klineage.memory.retrieve, then check their textual
preconditions and body against actual current source: types, layout/contiguity and
parallel ownership, storage placement, pipeline stages/ordering, hardware features,
conflicts, and optimizations already present. Enforce scope and
excluded IDs. No SKILL.md is valid only if no card applies; require a source-grounded
explanation of rejections. Otherwise require SKILL.md to restore
exactly one supplied eligible SkillCard, with all metadata and body unchanged.

Check the NCU request against the current fingerprint and problem, and the ranking
rationale against captured rows. Read current_kernel/evaluations/ncu-* (this workdir
for inline input). Missing/stale measurements or unsupported claims mean false.

